# Local-only material (personal notes, art, pasted references) — never tracked
docs-local/

# Generated QA artifacts — rebuilt by tools/optimize.mjs and tools/audit-effects.mjs
docs/meta-validation.md
docs/effect-audit.md

# Timing extraction intermediates — multi-MB, and regenerable ONLY from the raw
# asset export in docs-local/ (itself untracked), so committing them would bloat
# the repo without making them reproducible for anyone else. The curated OUTPUT,
# data/actionable-times.json, IS committed: tools/preprocess.mjs reads it to
# stamp real actionableAt values, so the build must not depend on the export.
# Same arrangement as data/forte-data.json. See docs/TIMING_MODEL.md.
data/timing-data.json
data/bullet-timings.json
docs/timing-extraction-report.md

# Python bytecode from the tools/extract/ asset readers.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
